Carrying those four items? No. :)

Getting disintegration resistance? Yes.

Realistically speaking you only need said resistance if you:

 a. don't have reflection (which is not really a safe long-term plan
    for anyone), or
 b. expect to get hit by a wide-angle disintegration beam.

The first I think can be called "one of the things that makes playing
a conduct monk challenging," and the second can be called "gross pilot
error." Yes, the change you suggest would make playing a vegetarian,
vegan, or foodless monk easier; but I don't think that particularly
needs to be made easier. Giving up meat should mean giving something up,
and right now that is:

 * 18/** strength (at least not without way more effort)
 * disintegration resistance
 * telepathy (except from prayer)
 * mind flayer int gain
 * probably something else, but not much

Now, you do have an argument you can make here. There is another way to
raise your INT and STR (in fact, more than one!) and another way to get
telepathy (divine gift), but there is no other way to get disintegration
resistance. I don't think there has to be, but if you want there to
be, I'd suggest that maybe it too should be a potential divine gift,
or maybe there should be a ring or amulet? Getting the intrinsic just
for leveling seems a bit too easy to me.

